#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Fundraising app: an organiser console, a public live display, and a "Fundraise Campaign" button
on the Apps menu.

    sudo python3 install-fundraise-app.py /opt/baja-apps

Writes three new modules:

    fundraise/console.js                 /app/fundraise/console
        Enter a campaign name and a dollar value ("$1,250", "1.2k", "2M" all read), optionally a goal,
        a donor count and a note. "Add a gift" adds to the running total and counts a donor. Publish
        writes the campaign into the owner's public folder, asks the server for a share code, and hands
        back the link, in the same share dialog the platform uses for a public LOH design. Below that, the campaign's details page: what the money is
        for, the donations as they come in, and dated updates you post during the event.

    manchester/viewer-fundraise.js       /app/manchester/viewer-fundraise?s=<code>
        What the room sees: title, the amount large enough to read across a hall, a thermometer against
        the goal, donors, and when it last moved. It animates the total upward rather than snapping, and
        re-reads every ten seconds (?refresh=<seconds>, 0 to stop). A "Campaign details" button opens
        the second level: the description, the updates and the recent donations. It is read-only, since
        this route is open without a sign-in, and a refresh that arrives while it is open redraws that
        page rather than throwing the reader back to the total. A "Donate" button, when the campaign
        has one, asks for an amount and hands the donor to Stripe: either a Checkout session created
        by POST /stripe/donation-session (a separate change to baja-server) or a Payment Link made in
        the Stripe dashboard. Which payment methods a donor sees is a Stripe dashboard setting, not a
        choice this page makes. No card detail is ever typed on this page, and a donation does not
        move the total by itself: the display asks the server to reconcile with Stripe before each
        re-read (POST /stripe/donation-sync, from install-donation-endpoint.py), and a paid donation
        then appears on its own within seconds. No sign-in: the Angular shell's auth
        guard lets through only URLs containing /manchester/viewer, which is why the display lives there.

    icons/svg/fundraise.js               a donation thermometer, for the launcher tile

and puts the button on three menus, each file backed up beside itself:

    manchester/fb.js                     the Apps menu on /app/baja/init, last in the list
    manchester/controls/baja-menu.js     the Baja menu, after Apps
    baja/applications.js                 the home launcher's Programme group

fb.js is patched by ANCHOR rather than by surrounding context: the deployed copy of that file is
known to differ from the repository's, so a context match would refuse on a file that is otherwise
exactly what we expect. The item goes in at the end of the Apps list, just before the Files & Folder
menu begins.

Every edit is worked out before anything is written, so a refusal leaves nothing half-installed.
Safe to run twice, and safe over the earlier version of this installer, which named the launcher
tile "Fundraising".
"""
import os, re, shutil, sys
